==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|keusanan|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|ǵews-|taste, choose|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''kiāsa'', Old Saxon [[kiosan]] (Dutch [[kiezen]]), Old High German [[kiosan]], Old Norse {{term|kjósa|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌺𐌹𐌿𐍃𐌰𐌽|tr=kiusan}}.  The Indo-European root was also the source of Latin {{term|gustus||taste|lang=la}}, Albanian {{term|desha||chosen|lang=sq}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtʃeːosɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
